8. An Easter problem

You are given a photograph taken on Easter Island. It shows what the island is best known for — one of its numerous stone moai statues. The photograph also shows stars; the equatorial coordinates of some of them are given in the table below. Note that the lowest bright point is a lantern, not a star or a reflection of anything in the water.

Determine (and be sure to describe the method of determination):

• the direction in which the camera was pointed when the picture was taken;

• the latitude of the island;

• the sidereal time of the moment the picture was taken;

• the date of the picture, assuming that the photograph was taken exactly at local solar midnight;

• the distance from the statue to the camera, if it is known that the width of the statue at the chest is 1.2 m.

